It's worth noting that the only modification the model made to improve itself was to reduce the length of its reasoning traces to avoid hitting the token limit. This is basically the same as the result from the recent weight-space programming article (
https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/
), which found that even Astra wasn't able to improve the performance of a model without this kind of obvious flaw.
